It follows that by differentiating the levers of statical stability and finding the slope at each ordinate the vertical distance of <math>\text{M}'</math> over <math>\text{G}</math> is obtained, and <math>\text{M}'</math> may be plotted by setting up this value from <math>\text{Z}'</math> above <math>\text{GZ}'</math> drawn at the correct inclination; also that by integrating the curve of statical stability and finding its area up to any angle, the vertical separation of <math>\text{G}</math> and <math>\text{B}'</math> is obtained, and <math>\text{B}'</math> may be plotted by setting down this value increased by <math>\text{BG}</math> below <math>\text{Z}'</math>.
